change_id: III-c7-02LK-24-positive-torsion-kernel
type: D02
statement_id: maps:src:D.2.43
old_location: S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III.tex (proof guard):lines 17831--17837
old_page: not asserted; exact released source interval
new_location: agents/continuation7_iii_general_cusp_receiving/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III_02LK_receiving.tex:lines 802--817
new_page: pending final III PDF build and page review
old_text: There is no hidden free-to-torsion extension
here: if a fibre-coinvariant element maps to
a torsion class, rational injectivity forces
that element itself to be torsion. Hence
the cap torsion is the image of the boundary
fibre torsion subgroup, not of a free class
whose rational image has been overlooked.
new_text: Consequently, after subtracting the two marked normal
images, any element of the entire boundary kernel comes
from the torsion subgroup in the first relative group. Its order is at most
\(s\). On the other hand \(a_0\) has exact order \(s\)
in the fibre coinvariants, by the unimodular six-bivector coordinates, and it
already vanishes in the cap. It therefore accounts for
the entire remaining kernel. We have proved the exact
marked identity
\[
 \ker\{H_2(M_L)\to H_2(N_L)\}
 =\mathbb Z\langle f_1\times\theta,f_2\times\theta\rangle
                  \oplus(\mathbb Z/s)\langle a_0\rangle.
\]
The inverse reads the Wang coordinates and then the
angular torsion coordinate in the six-bivector basis. This argument also
includes \(s=1\), where the last summand is zero.
reason: Replace the defensive paragraph by the full integral relative-group argument and exact boundary kernel.
review_status: local whole comparison complete; root admission and final page review pending

DEFECT 25 all eleven serialized fields
change_id: III-c7-02LK-25-positive-lattice-quotient
type: D02
statement_id: maps:src:D.2.43
old_location: S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III.tex (proof guard):lines 17845--17847
old_page: not asserted; exact released source interval
new_location: agents/continuation7_iii_general_cusp_receiving/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III_02LK_receiving.tex:lines 825--832
new_page: pending final III PDF build and page review
old_text: This proves exactly
\eqref{maps:eq:D.GC2}, not its saturation, and gives all
the remaining assertions in \eqref{maps:eq:D.GC3}.
new_text: In the Smith coordinates it is
\(\mathbb Z a_0+s\mathbb Z b_0\).
Its inverse relation coordinates read the \(a_0\)
coordinate and divide the \(b_0\) coordinate by \(s\)
on this image. The quotient map kills \(a_0\), reduces
the \(b_0\) coordinate modulo \(s\), and keeps the four
free coordinates in the six-bivector basis. Its inverse uses those
six-bivector representatives.
reason: Give the kernel coordinates, quotient and inverse representatives directly.
